[size=4][b]Priority Splitters[/b][/size]

Splitters in Moon Sweepers always alternate: one capsule left, one right, no matter what is waiting on either side. Mergers do the same with their inputs. That makes it impossible to say "feed the press first and only send the overflow to storage", or "always let the main line through and squeeze the side line in when there is room".

This mod gives every splitter a [b]priority output[/b] and every merger a [b]priority input[/b]. Walk up to a machine with the hammer out, press [b]P[/b], and it cycles through [b]left first[/b], [b]right first[/b] and back to the vanilla [b]round-robin[/b]. The S cone on a splitter and the M cone on a merger lean toward the priority lane so you can read the setting from across the base. Machines you never touch keep behaving exactly like vanilla.

[size=3][b]How it works[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Splitter, left first:[/b] every capsule goes left. Only while the left belt is backed up (a capsule standing still at its end) do capsules overflow to the right. As soon as the left lane moves again, it takes priority back.
[*][b]Merger, left first:[/b] while anything is waiting at the end of the left belt, the left belt goes in. The right belt only enters while the left end is empty.
[*][b]Round-robin:[/b] the vanilla behaviour, unchanged.
[*][b]Left and right[/b] are as seen looking along the direction the capsules travel.
[/list]

A backed-up lane is detected from the capsules themselves, not from a counter, so belts that feed machines, other splitters, mergers or dead ends all work the same way. Two tuning values decide how long a capsule has to stand still before its lane counts as blocked and how long it has to keep moving before the lane counts as free again, so a lane that inches forward stays "blocked" instead of flickering.

[size=3][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx 6.0.0-be.791 (Unity.IL2CPP win-x64) and the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/moonsweepers/mods/9]Moon Sweepers BepInEx Patcher[/url] first. Stock BepInEx cannot load plugins on this game without the patcher.
[*]Extract this mod into the game folder (where MoonSweepers.exe is), so the DLL ends up at [b]BepInEx\plugins\PrioritySplitters\PrioritySplitters.dll[/b].
[*]Start the game and load a save. Take out the hammer and look at a splitter or merger from within 6 m; the game's key prompt shows [b]P  Change priority[/b] with the current setting. Press P to cycle it.
[/list]

To uninstall, delete the BepInEx\plugins\PrioritySplitters folder. Your saves are untouched: priorities are stored next to the BepInEx config, not in the save file, and the machines simply go back to round-robin.

[size=3][b]Main features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Priority output per splitter and priority input per merger, toggled in game with one key while the hammer is out.
[*]The S and M cones lean toward the priority lane; round-robin machines stand upright.
[*]The game's own key prompt shows the toggle key and the current priority while you look at a machine in reach.
[*]Settings are remembered per save slot (BepInEx\config\PrioritySplitters\slot-N.json), so each save keeps its own layout.
[*]Vanilla routing for every machine you have not toggled, and an Enabled switch to turn the whole mod off without uninstalling.
[/list]

Settings in BepInEx\config\danbopes.moonsweepers.prioritysplitters.cfg (created on first start):

[list]
[*][b]ToggleKey[/b] - key that cycles the priority of the machine you are looking at (default p).
[*][b]HammerOnly[/b] - only toggle a machine, and only show its prompt, while the hammer is in hand (default on).
[*][b]ReachMeters[/b] - how close you have to be to toggle a machine and to see its prompt (default 6).
[*][b]LeanDegrees[/b] - how far the S and M cones lean (default 20; 0 hides the indicator).
[*][b]ShowPrompt[/b] - show the key prompt (default on).
[*][b]GraceSeconds[/b] - how long a capsule must stand still before its lane counts as backed up (default 0.2).
[*][b]ReleaseSeconds[/b] - how long a lane must keep moving before it counts as free again (default 1.0).
[*][b]Enabled[/b] - set to false for vanilla behaviour everywhere.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/moonsweepers/mods/9]Moon Sweepers BepInEx Patcher[/url]: required.
[*]BepInEx 6.0.0-be.791, Unity.IL2CPP win-x64: [url=https://builds.bepinex.dev/projects/bepinex_be]https://builds.bepinex.dev/projects/bepinex_be[/url]
[*]The current Steam version of Moon Sweepers (built and tested on 1.0.4). Works on Windows and under Proton on Linux.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Notes[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]A priority can only be chosen once both lanes of the machine have a belt attached; until then P reports round-robin.
[*]Co-op has not been tested. Routing happens in the simulation, so at least the host should have the mod installed.
[*]Nothing in the save file is changed. Removing the mod is safe at any time.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Source[/b][/size]

The mod is open source: [url=https://github.com/danbopes/MoonSweepers-PrioritySplitters]github.com/danbopes/MoonSweepers-PrioritySplitters[/url]. Bug reports and pull requests are welcome there.

